Abstract = {The purpose of this study is to illustrate an approach to generate one
   kilometer area percentage data model and generate one kilometer area
   percentage dataset on land uses based on the remotely sensed digital
   images to examine the changes of forest areas in the Northeast China
   during 1987-2000, and to find the spatio-temporal characteristics of
   land conversions between forest and other land uses and internal
   conversions of forest areas. Data was derived from Landsat TM/ETM bands
   3, 5 and 4 images acquired in 1987, 1995 and 2000, by the method of
   visual interpretation and Geographic Information System (GIS). The
   results showed that from 1987 to 2000, forests in Northeast China have
   undergone dramatic changes. 1.85 million ha of forest cover was lost due
   to the conversions of forest areas to other land uses while at the same
   time the forestry area also gained 0.47 million ha coming from other
   land uses. The Greater Hinggan Mountains forest region witnessed large
   amount of conversion from forest to cultivated lands, much of which has
   gone undetected by large-scale statewide inventories. Forest loss in the
   Northeast China Plain was mainly contributed to urban encroachment.
   These results demonstrate the need for more detailed and
   multidisciplinary research at smaller scales so as to enhance the
   understanding of the spatial patterns of forest cover changes.},
