   Sciences and Arts (SGEM 2014), Albena, BULGARIA, SEP 01-10, 2014},
Organization = {Bulgarian Acad Sci; Acad Sci Czech Republ; Latvian Acad Sci; Polish Acad
   Sci; Russian Acad Sci; Serbian Acad Sci \& Arts; Slovak Acad Sci Intro;
   Natl Acad Sci Ukraine; Natl Acad Sci Armenia; Sci Counc Japan; World
   Acad Sci TWAS; European Acad Sci, Arts \& Lett; Acad Fine Arts Zagreb
   Croatia; Croatian Acad Sci \& Arts; Acad Sci Moldova; Montenegrin Acad
   Sci \& Arts; Georgian Acad Sci; Acad Fine Arts \& Design Bratislava;
   Russian Acad Arts; Turkish Acad Sci; SGEM},
Abstract = {Nowadays there is a growing trend of aging population in the whole
   world, which occurs due to the reduction of fertility in developed
   countries and to increase life expectancy. By 2050 more than a quarter
   of the world population will be aging people. Therefore becomes relevant
   to examine the factors that provide life satisfaction and well-being of
   older people.
   These reasons have caused the proposal of the research to identify the
   key factors that determine the emotional well-being of aging people.
   The methodology of research is sociological survey, which was conducted
   by questionnaire prepared by the authors. For data processing there was
   used the method of mathematical analysis on the basis of the Spearman
   correlation coefficient.
   Subject area research focuses on theoretical and empirical analysis of
   the integrated construct emotional well-being, on the identification of
   the parameters of emotional well-being of aging people, the factors
   affecting the quality of emotional experience. Key indicators of
   emotional well-being were identified, on the basis of which the research
   tool (questionnaire) was developed. The approaches and understanding of
   the content category emotional well-being were found out.
   Results: 1) peculiarities in aging people emotional well-being were
   determined; 2) results of the survey were presented and analyzed; 3)
   correlation emotional well-being with different variables was
   identified.
   In conclusion it can be stated that active perception of life and
   environment has a positive impact on a person's life quality, duration
   of a healthy life period when people do not require help, creates a
   positive effect in the perception of old age. Therefore it is very
   important to continue in old age to awaken the desire to learn new
   things, stimulate the imagination and curiosity.},
