Organization = {Assoc Comp Machinery; ACM SIGCHI; Bold Insight UK; Eindhoven Univ
   Technol, Eindhoven AI Syst Inst; HMD Res},
Abstract = {During their information seeking people tend to filter out all the parts
   of the available information that do not fit their existing beliefs or
   opinions. In this paper we present a model for this ``Self-imposed
   Filter Bubble{''} (SFB) consisting of four dimensions. Thereby, we aim
   to 1) estimate the probability of the user being caught in an SFB and
   consequently, 2) identify suitable clues to reduce this probability in
   the further course of a dialogue. Using an exemplary implementation in
   an argumentative dialogue system, we demonstrate the validity and
   applicability of this model in an online user study with 102
   participants. These findings serve as a basis for developing a system
   strategy to break the user's SFB and contribute to a sustainable and
   profound reflection on a topic from all viewpoints.},
