   Special Programme Res, Dev \& Res Training Human Reproduct},
Abstract = {This paper provides an overview of what is known about the perspectives
   of women and men on methods of fertility regulation and identifies the
   knowledge gaps. The relevant literature is reviewed and supplemented
   with some additional analysis of data from the Demographic and Health
   Surveys (DHS). The discussion pertains to developing countries only,
   except for a few references to the prevalence of contraceptive use in
   developed countries: to methods of fertility regulation which are
   currently available rather than methods under development, and to
   women's and men's perspectives on contraceptive technology and not on
   the services delivering these technologies. The focus is on perceptions
   and perspectives, rather than with their determinants.},
