   Vehicles: A Literature Review and Perspectives},
Booktitle = {PROCEEDINGS OF THE 22ND CONGRESS OF THE INTERNATIONAL ERGONOMICS
   ASSOCIATION, VOL 4, IEA 2024},
Series = {Springer Series in Design and Innovation},
Year = {2025},
Volume = {56},
Pages = {187-192},
Note = {22nd Congress of the International Ergonomics Association-IEA, SOUTH
   KOREA, AUG 25-29, 2024},
Abstract = {Automated vehicles at SAE Level 4 and 5 no longer demand an onboard
   driver, but may require the assistance of remote operators in certain
   situations. Consequently, it is imperative to examine the qualifications
   and competencies of remote operators to ensure effective performance.
   Based on a comprehensive literature review, this paper compares the
   conventional driving task with the tasks of re-mote operators and
   identifies relevant qualifications and competencies. Further-more, this
   paper identifies potential for technological support to assist the
   remote operator in the perception and assessment of information, as well
   as in the execution of actions. Since the results are solely derived
   from a literature analysis, they require further evaluation through
   subject tests.},
