   GTR NRS},
Year = {2006},
Number = {P-14},
Pages = {459+},
Note = {Northeastern Recreation Research Symposium, Bolton Landing, NY, APR
   09-11, 2006},
Organization = {USDA Forest Serv; Venture Publishing},
Abstract = {We explored selected socio-demographic factors that influence the
   perception of constraints to art museum attendance among a sample of
   interested individuals who were currently not enjoying art museum
   visitation. Data from the Survey of Public Participation in the Arts
   (SPPA), a nationwide survey were used for this study. Using multivariate
   analysis of variance, we examined five main effects (gender, age,
   income, number of children, and place of residence) and all two-way
   interactions on two dimensions of constraints, internal and external.
   Our findings illustrated that perceived constraints to art museum
   visitation were a function of not only separate but also interactive
   effects of the socio-demographic factors. Implications for both
   constraints theory and practice are discussed.},
