   ADELAIDE, AUSTRALIA, OCT 02-07, 1994},
Organization = {Int Assoc Water Qual; Austr Water \& Wastewater Assoc, S Austr Branch;
   Austr Ctr Water Qual Res},
Abstract = {If consumers detect an off-flavor in their drinking water, they are
   likely to believe that it probably is nor safe. Water utilities will be
   defeating their best efforts to provide safe drinking water if they only
   meet health-related regulations and do not provide water that is free of
   off-flavor problems. The purpose of this paper is to explore the current
   U.S. regulatory environment and discuss how these regulations can
   adversely impact the control of off-flavors in drinking water. Utilities
   should adopt a water quality goal that allows them to not only meet the
   minimums of the regulations, but also meet the customer's highest
   standards - water that is free of off-flavors.},
