   Kingdom Int Grp},
Abstract = {Each year the Florida Department of Transportation, Metropolitan
   Planning Organizations (MPO), and City/County Governments are given the
   unenviable task of developing a priority list of transportation projects
   (i.e, roadway, air, bridge, rail, bike/pedestrian, etc.) to be included
   in the Tentative Work Program. Often there is controversy between the
   government agencies, as well as the general public as to where a
   specific project should fall on the list because of potential land use
   and environment priorities and concerns. To date, a good mechanism has
   not been developed for analyzing and presenting both the costs and
   benefits of a given project to all concerned parties. The objective of
   this project is to develop and demonstrate an Intermodal Transportation
   Planning Decision Support and Visualization System (ITP-DSVS). The
   purpose of the system is to aid State DOTS, MPOs, and City/County
   governments in assessing potential projects and developing priority
   lists. The system, consisting of modeling, mapping, data analysis, and
   visualization subsystems, is intended to provide FDOT, MPOs, and
   City/County governments with some technology tools that can help in
   meeting the requirements for comprehensive planning.},
Publisher = {AMER SOC CIVIL ENGINEERS},
